From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 22:01:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00877/11362] [outer-loop] Phase 1 v1: INCONCLUSIVE -- gold
 control ALSO degraded (harness over-fits, not the selector)

GSM8K (verified headroom, base 0.30 on the n=30 eval slice / 0.49 full). All 3 training
arms DROPPED below base: process_weighted 0.167, gold-UB 0.200, unweighted 0.200. The
GOLD positive control failing (-0.10) means the HARNESS degrades the model regardless of
selector -- full-FT a 1B on ~450-540 OFF-POLICY traces (2 epochs, lr 1e-5) catastrophically
forgets / overfits to another model's trace style. Same as Sudoku #4 v1 before the deep-sup
+ anchor fix. NOT a clean negative for process-reward -- untestable until the harness stops
degrading base. v2 fixes (mirroring #4 v2): LoRA or much lower LR + fewer steps + replay/
anti-forgetting; ideally ON-POLICY (MiniCPM's own traces) to remove the distribution shift.
Also: eval max_new_tokens=256 may truncate solutions (base 0.30 vs headroom 0.49) -> raise it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
